    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "***1 BEDROOM APARTMENT / PRIME CITY CENTRE LOCATION / IDEAL FOR OWNER OCCUPIERS OR INVESTORS / WALKING DISTANCE TO THE IFSC***\r\n\r\nKELLY BRADSHAW are delighted to present Apartment 26, Stapleton House, Mountjoy Square, Dublin 1\r\n\r\nSituated in the heart of Dublin City Centre, Apartment 26, Stapleton House is a superb one-bedroom residence offering bright, well-proportioned accommodation in a highly sought-after location. Positioned on the ground floor of this established development overlooking Mountjoy Square, the property presents an excellent opportunity for first-time buyers, investors, or those seeking a convenient city-centre home.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation briefly comprises an inviting entrance hallway leading to a spacious living and dining area, complete with wood-effect laminate flooring and a feature fireplace, creating a warm and comfortable living space. A separate fully fitted kitchen offers an excellent range of wall and floor units with ample storage and preparation space. The generous double bedroom benefits from fitted wardrobes, while the fully tiled bathroom is finished with a modern shower enclosure.\r\n\r\nPresented in good condition throughout, Apartment 26 enjoys an abundance of natural light and offers comfortable, low-maintenance living in one of Dublin's most convenient locations.\r\n\r\nThe property is ideally positioned within walking distance of Dublin's principal business, retail and leisure districts. The International Financial Services Centre (IFSC), O'Connell Street, Mater Hospital, Croke Park and Dublin's vibrant Docklands are all easily accessible, making this an ideal base for  working in the city. Residents benefit from a wealth of nearby amenities including cafés, restaurants, shops, parks and cultural attractions.\r\n\r\nExcellent transport links are available on the doorstep, with numerous Dublin Bus routes and LUAS services providing easy access throughout the city and beyond."
      },
